{"text": "Henry \u201cHank\u201d Hill\n\nPanama City, FL\n\nExperience\n\nAug. 2015 to\npresent\n\nOct. 2011 to\nAug. 2015\n\nBoys & Girls Clubs of Bay County, Inc\u2019\nChief Executive Officer\nFollowing the tenure of a 25 year veteran CEO, I took over an organization that has a rich history\nand yet a culture not used to change or growth. My top priority was to invest in the technology\nneeded both inside the corporate office as well as inside our unit offices so as to enable the\norganization to quickly focus on impact for our club members. Secondly, I established a culture\nof accountability with staff to drive impact as well as established staff development goals to\nequip them with the tools they need to succeed. Well versed in change management, [have\nsuccessfully lead the Board of Directors through a Strategic Plan that will strengthen the\norganization and mission. I developed and implemented an organizational realignment so as to\nmaximize resources where needed and to better position the organization to implement that plan.\n\nMastery Level Advanced Executive Leadership\nAttended Harvard Business School of Executive Leadership\nGoverning Board Member of Alignment Bay County Collaborative\nFSU-Panama City Community Partner- Recreation, Tourism, & Events\n\nBoys & Girls Clubs of the Cumberland Plateau\nChief Executive Officer\n\nTwas led to rural Appalachia Tennessee to restore confidence in the organization and to establish\nleadership and direction for a financially weakened non-profit struggling to achieve its mission,\nFirst, [completely tured the results of our annual audit around with a demonstrated ability to\norganize, direct, and create procedures to establish transparency & accountability as well as to\nrestore confidence from the community and our donors. Secondly, I worked closely with the\nboard to strategically identify, and recruit board members that immediately brought impact to our\nability to achieve our mission. Lastly, I created an outcome driven club environment focusing on\nAcademic Success, Healthy Lifestyles, and Character & Civic Engagement for our members. T\nhired, trained, and motivated quality staff while replacing those whom failed to meet standards. 1\norganized a complete overhaul of our technology lab, employee workstations, and network\nservers by an innovative grant and a strategic partnership with a local business. Under my\ndirection and stewardship, we operated a 45,000 square foot facility and a school based site in a\ncounty that suffered from the highest unemployment in the state.\n\n\u2018Completed Executive Advance Leadership Program (ALP) with BGCA\nServes on the Oneida Elementary Advisory Board & Scott County Chamber of Commerce\nServed on steering committee for the Tennessee All Staff Conference",
